Subject: [PATCH] Unsound diagnostic: the fold's error as BEEP's, to size a
 small-field proof

Not a sound configuration. For sizing only.

Under WHIR_DIAG_BEEP the per-step proximity-gaps error is taken as
2/|F|, BEEP's folding error with affine folding challenges (ePrint
2026/2930, Theorem 5.3), in place of the correlated-agreement bound.
That bound is about 87 bits over Goldilocks's quadratic extension, and
the configuration would otherwise grind for the rest. BEEP's samples
are not sent.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/protocols/params/regime.rs | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/protocols/params/regime.rs b/src/protocols/params/regime.rs
index 9c808d6..297bb91 100644
--- a/src/protocols/params/regime.rs
+++ b/src/protocols/params/regime.rs
@@ -106,6 +106,13 @@ impl DecodingRegimeParams {
     ///   `ε ≈ (2·10.5⁵/3) · n · ρ^{−3/2} / |F|`.
     /// - Capacity: STIR Conj 5.6, `ε ≈ d / (η · ρ²) / |F|`.
     pub fn eps_mca_log2(self, log_inv_rate: f64, message_length: usize, field_bits: f64) -> f64 {
+        // DIAGNOSTIC ONLY: under WHIR_DIAG_BEEP the fold's error is taken as BEEP's with affine
+        // folding challenges, 2/|F| (ePrint 2026/2930, Theorem 5.3), in place of the
+        // correlated-agreement bound, to size a proof in a field that bound cannot serve.
+        // Not a sound configuration of this code: BEEP's samples are not sent.
+        if std::env::var("WHIR_DIAG_BEEP").is_ok() {
+            return 1.0 - field_bits;
+        }
         let log_k = usize_to_f64(message_length).log2();
